WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
This show contains scenes that some viewers may
find disturbing.​ Viewer discretion ​is ​advised.

00:02.870 --> 00:04.750
Take that! And that!

00:04.750 --> 00:06.560
Get away from her!

00:11.280 --> 00:12.820
Take that! And that!

00:14.020 --> 00:15.530
You're in my way!

00:25.440 --> 00:27.030
R... Run....

00:32.320 --> 00:34.440
Forgive me! Are you all right?

00:35.200 --> 00:36.940
Wh-Why...

00:39.030 --> 00:42.990
O... merciful... Earth Mother...

01:04.680 --> 01:06.050
That's one...

01:13.990 --> 01:15.270
And that makes two.

01:16.710 --> 01:18.890
Um... Who are you?

01:25.840 --> 01:27.600
Goblin Slayer.

03:09.980 --> 03:14.900
<b>An Ordinary Spring Day</b>

03:46.660 --> 03:51.240
Next, number 15.
Please come up to reception.

03:51.240 --> 03:52.610
I've got a quest here!

03:52.610 --> 03:54.910
Seems a horde of dung-eaters
appeared in the sewers!

03:54.520 --> 03:56.400
Do you have your weapon and equipment ready?

03:54.910 --> 03:56.400
Anyone got some time?

03:56.400 --> 03:57.870
Did you memorize your spells?

03:57.870 --> 03:59.360
Yeah, of course.

03:59.360 --> 04:00.410
Okay, let's go!

04:05.110 --> 04:07.130
Well, aren't you in a good mood?

04:07.130 --> 04:09.810
This is my second year, after all!

04:09.810 --> 04:12.600
People can consider me 
their senior now, right?

04:12.600 --> 04:15.230
Wow, it's already been that long?

04:15.230 --> 04:20.800
Yes! And I was thinking I should be able
to rank up from 9th to 8th any day now.

04:20.800 --> 04:23.240
Well, you did work hard.

04:24.260 --> 04:27.510
Anyway, it sure is lively in here.

04:27.870 --> 04:30.220
Those girls are cute.

04:30.220 --> 04:34.250
I bet we can be friends with girls
like them if we become adventurers!

04:34.250 --> 04:39.450
Seriously? Do they really think
they can keep secrets around elves?

04:39.450 --> 04:42.970
I was lined up over there last year, too,

04:43.330 --> 04:45.970
but there weren't this many then.

04:45.970 --> 04:49.620
And that's probably exactly why
a training center's opening up.

04:49.620 --> 04:51.210
Did you read the letter?

04:51.210 --> 04:54.400
Yup, I sure did! Of course.

04:54.400 --> 04:57.340
Setting up a charity for new adventurers...

04:57.340 --> 04:59.040
She sure works fast.

04:59.040 --> 05:00.860
Yes, truly.

05:00.860 --> 05:06.760
She said she wanted to help as support 
from now on rather than be an adventurer.

05:08.070 --> 05:10.470
I'm glad she seems to be doing well.

05:10.470 --> 05:12.860
I heard she made amends with her family, too.

05:14.000 --> 05:15.450
All right, let's go.

05:18.740 --> 05:23.770
Whether you can learn something in 
the beginning or not really is important.

05:24.880 --> 05:28.810
I don't think it's that deep.

05:28.810 --> 05:34.310
I mean, there are some people who never
listen, no matter what they learn.

05:34.310 --> 05:37.050
For example, dwarves.

05:37.050 --> 05:39.940
I can hear you, long-ears.

05:39.940 --> 05:44.000
Actually, it's you elves who never listen.

05:44.000 --> 05:47.350
Now, now. Our hearing is far 
superior to that of dwarves.

05:47.350 --> 05:50.720
You see? Anvils don't get sarcasm.

05:50.720 --> 05:52.240
Who are you calling an anvil?!

05:52.240 --> 05:55.670
Well, I don't see anyone else who fits the bill.

05:54.770 --> 05:57.570
How peaceful.

05:57.570 --> 05:59.220
Don't get too rowdy.

05:59.220 --> 06:01.770
Otherwise, we won't look as
cool in front of the rookies.

06:01.920 --> 06:05.760
See? Interactions like that
lead to better teamwork.

06:05.920 --> 06:09.130
You're just making excuses for being
a violent drunk. Okay, lawful good.

06:09.300 --> 06:10.180
Heya!

06:10.330 --> 06:11.600
Good morning!

06:11.720 --> 06:12.600
Good luck today!

06:12.720 --> 06:13.650
Yo!

06:13.650 --> 06:16.640
Hey! Greet them properly!

06:16.640 --> 06:18.030
Hello there.

06:18.790 --> 06:22.450
You all seem to be in good 
spirits since it got warmer.

06:22.450 --> 06:25.570
I also love the warm weather.

06:25.570 --> 06:28.130
Winter did seem harsh for you.

06:28.130 --> 06:29.350
Indeed.

06:29.350 --> 06:31.990
So, where is Goblin Slayer?

06:31.990 --> 06:33.970
He said he was going to be a little late.

06:34.280 --> 06:36.510
He should be here soon, though.

06:42.640 --> 06:43.580
What the...

06:46.490 --> 06:48.060
Goblin Slayer!

06:48.910 --> 06:50.760
Goblin Slayer?

06:50.760 --> 06:53.800
Slayer of goblins? What the heck?

06:54.900 --> 06:56.550
So you're all here already.

06:56.550 --> 06:58.800
You're the one who's late, Orcbolg!

06:58.800 --> 07:00.850
So, what are we doing today?

07:01.440 --> 07:02.960
Slaying goblins.

07:02.960 --> 07:04.650
Figured as much.

07:04.650 --> 07:06.670
I'll listen to your requests if you have any.

07:06.670 --> 07:11.470
As long as we do something pious,
I am willing to do anything.

07:13.200 --> 07:16.310
Okay, fine! Fine!

07:16.310 --> 07:20.000
We can go hunt some goblins.

07:20.470 --> 07:21.450
Thanks.

07:24.550 --> 07:28.110
Heya, Goblin Slayer. Slaying goblins again?

07:28.110 --> 07:29.690
Yeah. Killing goblins.

07:29.690 --> 07:31.090
Never get bored of that, do ya?

07:31.090 --> 07:34.950
We've got a long trip ahead of us.
We're gonna explore some ruins.

07:34.950 --> 07:36.110
I see.

07:34.950 --> 07:37.040
Hey, he's...

07:36.110 --> 07:37.040
Take care out there.

07:37.040 --> 07:38.110
I will.

07:37.040 --> 07:38.890
Yeah...

07:40.100 --> 07:42.100
What are they saying?

07:42.100 --> 07:44.350
You're better off not knowing.

07:47.840 --> 07:50.070
Goblins. You got any?

07:51.600 --> 07:52.780
But of course!

07:55.280 --> 07:57.560
That's a lot of quests.

07:57.560 --> 08:00.500
Probably because it's spring.

08:00.500 --> 08:04.390
And that's after all the 
rookies took some, actually.

08:05.100 --> 08:06.290
Can they handle them?

08:08.640 --> 08:10.750
Show me those that have
already been accepted, too.

08:12.790 --> 08:14.650
Can you handle all of these?

08:14.650 --> 08:15.760
That's fine.

08:15.760 --> 08:18.340
Hey, we should probably get some potions.

08:18.340 --> 08:19.950
But those cost money...

08:19.950 --> 08:21.850
We'd probably only be able to buy one.

08:19.950 --> 08:21.850
I'll take care of these in this order.

08:21.850 --> 08:25.770
Understood. Oh, do you need any potions?

08:26.610 --> 08:30.990
I'll need Heal, Antidote,
and Stamina. Six of each.

08:30.990 --> 08:31.820
You got it!

08:32.170 --> 08:32.990
Whoa...

08:36.000 --> 08:37.440
Whatcha doin'?

08:37.440 --> 08:40.520
Making sure I don't mistake them 
by just touching the bottles.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.710
Oh, I'll help.

08:42.710 --> 08:43.830
Thanks.

08:43.830 --> 08:45.330
Mine!

08:45.330 --> 08:49.210
Long-ears, show a little more restraint.

08:49.210 --> 08:52.660
Don't worry. I'm not stingy like you dwarves.

08:56.010 --> 08:57.560
I don't really need that.

08:57.560 --> 08:59.260
Well, too bad.

09:00.170 --> 09:03.980
We've got to handle our money and
items properly among our party.

09:04.220 --> 09:05.480
I'd like to take a look, as well.

09:05.480 --> 09:08.560
U-Um... What are you doing?

09:14.270 --> 09:15.990
Well, you see...

09:15.990 --> 09:20.010
We're marking the potions so we don't
mistakenly pull out the wrong ones.

09:20.010 --> 09:21.340
You're marking them?

09:21.340 --> 09:25.850
You may not always have time to check
which one you have before using it.

09:25.850 --> 09:27.150
Oh, I see.

09:27.150 --> 09:28.460
You know,

09:28.680 --> 09:31.610
just labeling everything won't 
help you remember what's what.

09:33.520 --> 09:37.060
Oh, come on. I wouldn't do that.

09:37.910 --> 09:40.480
Limit it to things you'll need to use in a hurry.

09:41.130 --> 09:42.350
Also...

09:42.350 --> 09:46.350
Be careful around goblins.
Start off by killing rats.

09:46.350 --> 09:50.010
Er, uh, r-right!
Got it... I mean, I understand.

09:52.860 --> 09:55.900
I hope they survive.

09:56.240 --> 09:57.490
Who knows?

09:57.490 --> 10:00.120
Goblin Slayer, here.

10:00.120 --> 10:01.080
Thanks.

10:03.160 --> 10:04.150
I took these.

10:07.980 --> 10:08.890
Well?

10:10.860 --> 10:12.090
What do you mean, "Well"?

10:12.090 --> 10:14.840
We're here because we
decided to come with you.

10:15.720 --> 10:19.260
You'll wander off on your own 
if we leave you alone, anyway.

10:19.260 --> 10:20.840
Also...

10:20.840 --> 10:24.190
You're way too unaware of
your surroundings, Orcbolg.

10:25.590 --> 10:29.850
You don't care that they've
been gossiping about you?

10:29.850 --> 10:35.700
No. I have no idea what they're
expecting from me, anyway.

10:36.060 --> 10:38.610
All right, Beard-cutter.

10:40.880 --> 10:42.700
Off we go to slay some goblins.

10:42.700 --> 10:45.040
Too right.

10:45.040 --> 10:48.330
Hey! You're in my way! You're gonna get hurt!

10:49.080 --> 10:50.800
I-I'm sorry.

10:50.800 --> 10:51.490
You're fine.

10:51.490 --> 10:53.210
Hey, be more careful, lad!

10:53.450 --> 10:54.880
Shut up!

10:54.880 --> 10:56.960
It's your fault for being so slow!

10:57.220 --> 10:59.090
Don't make me throw a fireball at you!

11:00.180 --> 11:02.990
Honestly, kids these days.

11:02.990 --> 11:06.060
Wow, spoken like a true old person, Dwarf.

11:06.060 --> 11:08.590
You're the last person I want 
to hear that from, Elf.

11:08.590 --> 11:10.260
What'd you say?!

11:10.930 --> 11:15.910
Well... The more rookies there are, the more
likely we are to see some rotten apples.

11:16.570 --> 11:18.570
Is something the matter?

11:18.570 --> 11:23.110
Oh, no. It's nothing... Really.

11:31.280 --> 11:33.170
A-Are we there?

11:33.170 --> 11:36.750
Yes, we are. We're here, long-ears.

11:36.970 --> 11:40.860
I don't think Priestess
can make it much further.

11:42.920 --> 11:46.660
Can we leave this to you, Sir Goblin Slayer?

11:46.660 --> 11:50.180
Yeah, I will. Take care of her.

11:50.430 --> 11:54.690
Ugh, I'm so tired. I'm going to sleep.

11:54.690 --> 11:56.440
Well, see you tomorrow.

11:56.890 --> 11:57.640
Yeah.

12:02.000 --> 12:03.160
Only the light is on?

12:05.740 --> 12:06.910
A goblin?

12:13.970 --> 12:16.650
You can sleep a little longer...

12:21.300 --> 12:23.320
I guess you're not a goblin.

12:24.910 --> 12:28.420
Huh?! O-Oh... G-Goblin Slayer.

12:29.260 --> 12:31.680
I wasn't asleep! I was <i>not</i> asleep, you hear me?!

12:35.760 --> 12:40.440
So, how did it go? That was
quite a few quests this time.

12:40.680 --> 12:42.700
Yeah, there were goblins.

12:42.700 --> 12:46.360
How many were there? Oh, please
list them off one quest at a time.

12:46.970 --> 12:50.420
The first one had 34. And then under ten.

12:50.420 --> 12:51.870
Under ten?

12:51.870 --> 12:55.520
I went under, saved the prisoners,
and destroyed the nest.

12:55.520 --> 12:57.910
I confirmed 34 corpses.

12:57.910 --> 12:59.250
The rest should be less than ten.

12:59.250 --> 13:02.760
Er... How about the second quest?

13:03.010 --> 13:04.390
There were goblins.

13:04.390 --> 13:06.380
I counted twenty and then three.

13:06.380 --> 13:10.510
I smoked them out, and once they emerged,
I destroyed the ceiling and crushed them.

13:11.970 --> 13:15.510
We did a pincer attack on those that 
remained and killed them one by one.

13:15.850 --> 13:18.460
The weapons I used belonged
to the dead goblins.

13:18.990 --> 13:19.980
Stop.

13:20.600 --> 13:25.700
What?! Even if goblins aren't a big
deal, it doesn't hurt to review...

13:25.700 --> 13:26.990
No.

13:26.990 --> 13:30.530
I'm saying you're through if the
goblins get a hold of your notes.

13:31.450 --> 13:36.210
A-Are you the one people call "Goblin Slayer"?

13:36.210 --> 13:37.670
They do call me that.

13:37.670 --> 13:41.440
In that case, teach me how to kill goblins!

13:41.440 --> 13:42.330
No.

13:42.940 --> 13:43.950
Why not?

13:43.950 --> 13:46.620
If you can't do something until you're taught,

13:46.620 --> 13:48.480
nothing will change, even if you are taught.

13:48.480 --> 13:49.210
Wha...

13:50.970 --> 13:53.490
Sorry to keep you up late. Thanks.

13:53.490 --> 13:56.520
Oh, it's fine. Thank you
for everything you do.

13:56.520 --> 13:58.420
Oh, as for your payment...

13:58.420 --> 14:01.490
Split it up. I'll just take my share for now.

14:01.490 --> 14:02.490
Sure thing.

14:04.770 --> 14:07.650
Remember the party that just
registered the other day?

14:07.650 --> 14:09.360
The one with the Rhea girl.

14:09.360 --> 14:10.410
Ah...

14:10.720 --> 14:11.900
Don't worry.

14:11.900 --> 14:15.620
I guess she did get bitten a little 
when she went to kill some rats...

14:15.620 --> 14:17.490
But she had an antidote.

14:17.490 --> 14:18.480
I see.

14:19.480 --> 14:21.220
Are you relieved?

14:21.220 --> 14:22.070
Yeah.

14:23.400 --> 14:24.420
Who is that?

14:24.420 --> 14:30.220
He just registered as an adventurer.
Apparently, he wants to hunt goblins on his own.

14:30.220 --> 14:32.830
On his own? That's ridiculous.

14:37.350 --> 14:39.620
Hey. Do you have a place to stay?

14:40.570 --> 14:42.160
That's none of your business.

14:42.160 --> 14:43.120
I see.

14:49.150 --> 14:50.170
Come with me.

14:51.610 --> 14:53.470
Hey, wait!

14:53.470 --> 14:54.990
You're not the boss of me!

14:58.130 --> 15:00.000
Thanks for the tea.

15:06.790 --> 15:09.520
Wh-What's the big idea? Hey!

15:09.520 --> 15:11.810
Where are you taking me?

15:12.590 --> 15:13.920
Come with me and you'll find out.

15:21.730 --> 15:24.010
A... farm?

15:28.910 --> 15:31.300
Oh, you're home!

15:34.200 --> 15:36.020
Welcome home!

15:37.450 --> 15:39.320
Yeah, I'm home.

15:39.320 --> 15:41.460
You took quite a while this time.

15:41.760 --> 15:43.960
How'd it go? Are you hurt at all?

15:46.190 --> 15:48.670
Who's this?

15:49.830 --> 15:53.180
I-I'm... a-an adventurer!

15:53.430 --> 15:56.250
He's a rookie. He has no place to stay.

15:56.250 --> 15:58.180
Oh, really?

15:59.540 --> 16:00.920
Huh...

16:00.920 --> 16:02.440
I see, I see.

16:02.830 --> 16:04.560
Sure, I don't mind.

16:04.560 --> 16:06.190
Thanks. That's a huge help.

16:06.190 --> 16:09.520
No worries. I'd expect this from you.

16:09.520 --> 16:12.770
I want to speak to your
uncle, too. Is he awake?

16:12.770 --> 16:13.880
Probably.

16:13.880 --> 16:14.810
I see.

16:15.850 --> 16:16.710
Hey.

16:17.870 --> 16:19.200
Are you his wife?

16:19.200 --> 16:20.280
Well, yeah.

16:20.280 --> 16:21.290
No.

16:21.290 --> 16:22.320
No.

16:22.320 --> 16:24.980
Aw, come on, Uncle.

16:24.980 --> 16:27.840
Letting him spend one night won't hurt.

16:29.210 --> 16:33.730
An adventurer who just registered
is no different from some ruffian.

16:33.730 --> 16:37.100
Wha— You're saying I'm
the same as some crook?!

16:37.680 --> 16:38.760
Be quiet.

16:41.370 --> 16:45.020
That attitude is precisely why no one's
going to trust you, myself included.

16:46.580 --> 16:50.110
Then what about the barn I'm renting?

16:51.320 --> 16:54.650
Are you able to take responsibility
if something happens to this kid?

16:54.650 --> 16:57.410
No. That's why I'm going to
stay up and keep watch.

17:02.410 --> 17:03.790
Uncle...

17:06.410 --> 17:08.460
All right, fine.

17:08.460 --> 17:10.820
In return, you need to actually sleep.

17:10.820 --> 17:13.700
Adventurers are nothing if
their bodies aren't healthy.

17:14.540 --> 17:17.560
Right. Thank you very much.

17:25.560 --> 17:29.150
Who the heck are those guys anyway?

17:29.480 --> 17:30.700
What do you mean?

17:30.700 --> 17:34.530
If she's not your wife,
they're not your family, are they?

17:35.730 --> 17:36.950
Yeah.

17:37.240 --> 17:39.060
I've known them forever.

17:39.060 --> 17:41.950
He's my landlord. And she's his daughter.

17:42.250 --> 17:44.290
That's who they are, objectively.

17:44.720 --> 17:47.960
I don't know how they view me.

17:47.960 --> 17:49.530
What's that even mean?

17:54.490 --> 17:55.970
You're not going to sleep?

17:56.370 --> 17:58.980
I can sleep with one eye open.

17:59.390 --> 18:01.350
So I can be prepared if a goblin shows up.

18:03.480 --> 18:04.850
What the heck?

18:05.530 --> 18:08.230
If you want to kill goblins,
you need to at least be able to do that.

18:08.230 --> 18:10.730
That's not even necessary.

18:11.060 --> 18:14.150
I see. If you don't think so, fine.

18:15.350 --> 18:20.090
Go to sleep. I'll see you to the
guild after breakfast tomorrow.

18:39.940 --> 18:43.050
You ate too much. Well, I'm going.

18:44.150 --> 18:50.310
First, you should go to the sewers
and kill some... you know, rats.

18:51.670 --> 18:57.400
I'm... going to hunt... goblins.

18:58.300 --> 18:59.130
I see.

19:06.090 --> 19:08.620
Goblin Slayer...

19:08.620 --> 19:10.000
What's the matter?

19:10.000 --> 19:12.830
She went to talk about
moving up a rank, and...

19:12.830 --> 19:18.550
I was told that I probably
haven't contributed enough.

19:18.550 --> 19:23.900
That cannot be helped. The rest
of us are all Silver-ranked.

19:23.900 --> 19:27.970
I wonder if they think
you're being carried by us.

19:29.280 --> 19:32.860
U-Um... Don't let this bother you.

19:33.210 --> 19:37.110
I think they'll acknowledge
me if I work harder.

19:37.440 --> 19:40.180
Hey, if rank is the issue,

19:40.180 --> 19:43.490
then why not go on a quest with some
Porcelain and Obsidian adventurers?

19:43.490 --> 19:44.870
Good point.

19:45.200 --> 19:47.950
I know! They just need to
see you mentor someone.

19:48.160 --> 19:49.950
U-Um...

19:50.330 --> 19:57.110
Does that mean I should adventure
with people other than all of you?

19:57.110 --> 20:00.170
Yeah. That's not a bad idea.

20:00.170 --> 20:03.490
Guess that's settled.
Let's find some Porcelain kid and—

20:04.760 --> 20:06.860
Even if you're just a rear guard,

20:06.860 --> 20:10.640
you'll never go up in rank if all you can 
do is shake and cower in the corner.

20:10.640 --> 20:13.440
I-I'm not cowering!

20:13.440 --> 20:14.830
Yeah, I don't know about that.

20:14.830 --> 20:18.960
I bet when you're in trouble, you're shaking
in your boots and just calling for God.

20:18.960 --> 20:23.400
Wha— That's not true! I do a lot of things...

20:24.750 --> 20:29.640
If you're going to judge others, then you
cannot complain if others judge you.

20:29.640 --> 20:31.430
Wh-What?

20:31.430 --> 20:37.180
To mock a single priest is the same 
as mocking a million priests.

20:37.180 --> 20:38.540
What's that brat's problem?

20:38.540 --> 20:39.580
Ignore him.

20:39.580 --> 20:43.150
I guess he's never been out in the
wasteland with no food or water.

20:43.150 --> 20:45.390
He'll understand once he 
gets himself nearly killed.

20:45.390 --> 20:46.560
Hey, you!

20:46.560 --> 20:50.390
Try saying all that again while
looking me right in the eye!

20:50.390 --> 20:53.460
Hey, stop that, you dummy.
Let's go kill some rats.

20:53.460 --> 20:56.650
Let go of me! Let go!

20:56.650 --> 21:01.320
W-Well... I'm an adventurer, too!

21:01.590 --> 21:03.510
Goblins are nothing!

21:03.510 --> 21:06.700
Goblin Slayer? Really?

21:06.700 --> 21:09.830
You tell me not to take notes, yet you 
won't share your goblin-hunting secrets,

21:10.160 --> 21:11.540
then you tell me to kill rats?

21:11.790 --> 21:13.040
Screw that!

21:13.300 --> 21:16.010
I'm gonna kill some goblins!

21:16.810 --> 21:18.250
Orcbolg...

21:19.110 --> 21:20.090
Is he your little brother?

21:20.090 --> 21:23.020
No. I only have an older sister.

21:23.020 --> 21:25.970
I see. So, who is this kid?

21:25.970 --> 21:28.900
He's a rookie. A wizard, apparently.

21:30.690 --> 21:32.830
I heard everything!

21:36.770 --> 21:38.100
Sorry...

21:38.100 --> 21:41.160
Who the heck are you? Butt out!

21:41.160 --> 21:42.860
Just listen a moment, boy.

21:42.860 --> 21:45.240
I have a good idea.

21:46.030 --> 21:48.890
Why don't you try and slay some goblins?

21:49.980 --> 21:51.950
B-Bring it on!

21:51.950 --> 21:53.460
But...

21:53.460 --> 21:56.040
The leader of your party is
going to be Priestess there.

21:57.190 --> 21:57.950
Huh?

21:59.020 --> 22:01.960
Wh-What?!

23:31.970 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time</b>

23:31.970 --> 23:40.250
<b>The Red-Headed Wizard Boy</b>
